{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 940e2dcaf0db2aaf68a03861a6977b2f909488b2 for Lane 0. Reviewed all 27 named artifacts using the complete earlier contract reviews plus the six-file repair diff. Detached worktree dependency install and strict workspace typecheck pass; all five compile-only examples are included.\n\nThe remaining P1 from d12b67d6 is resolved at the contract boundary. R-ADM-3(c) now requires the invitation's recorded custody to match the trusted AdmissionPath. R-ADM-12 covers RPC submit, HTTPS /acts and client redemption as submitted, and permits room-redemption only inside the room's own key-generating/holding operation. Caller fields cannot supply that internal privilege. Cross-custody joins refuse with custody-mismatch before recording or consumption, including both directions. Authority records the matched custody for later verification, and the normative table explicitly exercises all four wrong-route cases plus successful bounded MCP redemption. Ordinary client joins, unjoined delegated Workers and recovery authority remain available.\n\nArchitecture: approved. There is one shared admission model, an acyclic signed-log construction, a complete platform-only configuration recovery workflow, and separate public operation/holder-only credential surfaces. Every act and refusal is projected from stable recorded events. Internal AdmissionPath stays outside the signed public wire shape.\nSecurity: approved for this types-only protocol delivery. The recipient of a room-custody invitation cannot install a caller-owned direct member key through another route under these rules. Runtime enforcement and cross-route regressions remain obligations for the Room/transport implementation. Historical evidence, compromise handling, check isolation, scoped global tests and the unresolved publication slot protections are preserved.\nSimplification: approved. A narrow internal custody condition and explicit acceptance cases close the issue without multiplying transport-specific authority models. The revised runtime-failure wording correctly separates admission from post-commit notification retries, and lost-response room redemption has a documented recovery route.\n\nScope/limits: this approves the Lane 0 contract, not deployed implementation behavior or the current Lane C runtime. The independent Lane C review found omitted replay context, mutable retained inputs, current-role rechecking of historical admin evidence, and arbitrary path-key hazards; its repair may require a later deliberate contract amendment (complete/versioned aggregate budget and replay context, safe path representation). That is ongoing tracked work, not a reason to hold this now-correct custody repair. Lane E must implement and test atomic/refused/partial/lost-response redemption and secret confinement, Lane D the normative authority/admission/log rules, and Lane C the recorded-input replay invariant. All requested functionality remains in scope; estimates do not constrain it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:39a45ac8ab9745c2e3faaafb368c99c7279f883a","binding":"assigned","head":"940e2dcaf0db2aaf68a03861a6977b2f909488b2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1aedc45f76089714510fa13c27053768c6265757\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a121cd85bf737bc30126316df28adf092ebacdc1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1aedc45f76089714510fa13c27053768c6265757","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}